+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"observation","id":"obs_01M2GMWPY9B54SGT32H9MFQ5KY","supersedes":"obs_01M2G2AGGSXWPRR33K23JB6E90","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T18:36:43Z","companyId":"example-co","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S1"],"title":"Credential handling is sound at process-config level but breaks at the tool-argument schema and dry-run debug path","description":"The keychain-backed redaction pipeline (parseUserConfig.ts registerKnownSecretsInRootKeychain, LoggerBase.redactIfNecessary) correctly protects process-level credentials in logs and telemetry. It does not cover: (1) the connect/switch-connection tool argument schemas, which expose a live mongodb:// connection string (typically credential-bearing) with no isSecret/classification metadata (connect.ts:13-15, switchConnection.ts:13-20); (2) DryRunModeRunner.dumpConfig() (dryModeRunner.ts:43-46), which prints the resolved UserConfig object, including apiClientSecret/connectionString/voyageApiKey, to stdout with no redaction call at all, a documented (server.json MDB_MCP_DRY_RUN) reachable code path. Commit aaa72a040db4c32f3d6488d5e28e2892a68e9ee0.","methods":["probe-schemas"],"subjects":[{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"}],"collectedAt":"2026-09-14T18:36:43Z","expiresAt":"2026-10-14T18:36:43Z","result":"partial","toolOutput":{"format":"sarif","path":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/2853edbc-3a09-4ec1-87ad-1afe187bb68c/probe-schemas.mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.sarif.export.json","sha256":"ac53f2a64f99af00b6ec6e40eb92f649a78ae68fbe90db7cc9f36ffe8a5c4e6c"},"evidence":[{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/src/tools/mongodb/connect/connect.ts","description":"argsShape.connectionString, lines 13-15"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/mcp-gateway/repos/mongodb-mcp-server/src/transports/dryModeRunner.ts","description":"dumpConfig(), lines 43-46"},{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/2853edbc-3a09-4ec1-87ad-1afe187bb68c/probe-