+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2GMWPZ5DKN7DNH3D65T47FZ","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T18:36:43Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"switch-connection tool's connectionString argument carries no isSecret/classification annotation","description":"SwitchConnectionTool.argsShape.connectionString (switchConnection.ts:13-20) has the same gap as the connect tool: z.string().optional().describe(...) only, no isSecret/classification metadata, so an MCP client can be handed a live mongodb:// URI (typically credential-bearing) through a tool schema with no indication it must be treated as a secret. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S1. SLA topic: patch-sla. Refutation: evidence lens not refuted (The cited evidence holds: switchConnection.ts lines 13-20 at pinnedCommit aaa72a04 define connectionString as z.string().optional().describe(...) only, with no register/isSecret, while the same codebase's userConfig.ts:40-46 registers the same field with isSecret:true (configUtils.ts:33 defines that key). The SARIF export exists at the cited path and has the matching SCH-API-06 fail result (level error, same path and lines, fingerprints maxwell/v1 fc0f2777...0466 equal to the candidate), its session id and run id match the context, and the message agrees with the description. Nothing in the repo offsets the gap: tool-argument connection strings are never added to the keychain (only connectCluster.ts and createDBUser.ts register user/password, and parseUserConfig.ts registers config values only), and deploy/aws/Dockerfile disables only atlas-local, so switch-connection stays enabled. The code is reachable in qa (internal) and prod (partner exposure), both classified pii and financial. Severity high equals the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S1, so it is not estimated. Side note outside this lens: dpdp-rules-2025 6(1)(a) is about masking personal data, not credentials, so its fit is weak. Unverifiable: sha256 ac53f2a6... cannot be computed here and matches only the caller-supplied sarifSha256.); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (The mapping holds and can be repaired: all three instruments apply to example-co, SEBI CSCRF PR.AA.S1 (credentials managed for processes) is a real, in-scope clause that covers the gap and is cited first, and severity high equals its catalog defaultSeverity (the SCH-API-06 rule has no security-severity score); however DPDP 6(1)(a) covers encrypting, masking or tokenising personal data, not handling a credential that grants access to a store holding personal data, so it is replaced with 6(1)(b) (access control on computer resources, control record present in the ledger) (unverifiable: OWASP ASVS 5.0 13.3.1 wording, no catalog file).).","severity":"high","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S1","dpdp-rules-2025:6(1)(b)"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.AA.S1"},{"regulator":"MeitY","instrument":"dpdp-rules-2025","controlId":"6(1)(b)"},{"regulator":"OWASP","instrument":"owasp-asvs-5.0","controlId":"13.3.1"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"},"location":{"path":"src/tools/mongodb/connect/switchConnection.ts","startLine":13,"endLine":20},"fingerprint":"fc0f2777b297788e9a70776540f747efe1d1655fe30086af4194f09ecd900466","source":{"kind":"sarif","ruleId":"SCH-API-06","tool":"maxwell-schema-auditor","toolVersion":"1.0.0"},"status":"open","firstSeenAt":"2026-09-14T18:36:43Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-09-14T18:36:43Z","slaBasis":{"instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.MA.S3","topic":"patch-sla","severity":"high","days":7},"slaDueAt":"2026-09-21T18:36:43Z","relatedObservationIds":["obs_01M2GMWPY9B54SGT32H9MFQ5KY","obs_01M2GMWPSGBCYNXA6S2ZR7ZT5R"],"evidence":[{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/2853edbc-3a09-4ec1-87ad-1afe187bb68c/probe-schemas.mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.sarif.export.json","sha256":"ac53f2a64f99af00b6ec6e40eb92f649a78ae68fb