+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2GPBK5MBCAFFV7KNH83JV1F","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T19:14:04Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"Elicitation-based approval for destructive MongoDB/Atlas tools auto-approves when the client omits elicitation support","description":"src/elicitation.ts Elicitation.requestConfirmation() (lines 30-33): `if (!this.supportsElicitation()) { return true; }` returns approved=true without ever prompting a human, before the call to server.elicitInput(). ToolBase.verifyConfirmed() in src/tools/tool.ts (lines 609-615) routes every tool named in userConfig.ts confirmationRequiredTools (drop-database, drop-collection, delete-many, drop-index, atlas-create-access-list, atlas-create-db-user, atlas-streams-manage, atlas-streams-teardown; userConfig.ts:79-94) through this same function, so any MCP client that simply does not declare the `elicitation` client capability executes these destructive operations with zero human approval. This is a deployed gateway ('mcp-gateway', README: 'lets ExampleCo's AI agents query the client-data and order stores') with qa/prod environments classified pii+financial (applications/mcp-gateway/env/qa.json, env/prod.json) and prod exposure 'partner'; company-profile/example-co/sdlc/policy.json aiCodingPolicy.humanReviewRequired is true and promptInjectionControls includes 'human-approval-for-writes'. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S3 (high). Refutation: evidence lens not refuted (Every cited fact checks out in files I opened: src/elicitation.ts lines 30-33 return true without prompting when the client lacks elicitation, tool.ts invoke() line 491-492 and verifyConfirmed() lines 609-615 send every confirmationRequiredTools entry through that function, userConfig.ts lines 79-90 default to exactly the 8 tools named, and nothing in the repo overrides this (deploy/aws/Dockerfile sets only MDB_MCP_DISABLED_TOOLS=atlas-local and never readOnly; the readOnly=true default in main.bicep is Azure-only while prod runs on EKS); the SARIF export has the matching AGENT-ASI09-01 fail result (index 0, src/elicitation.ts 30-44, same fingerprint), prod.json shows exposure partner with pii+financial, qa.json shows pii+financial, policy.json has humanReviewRequired true and human-approval-for-writes, and high equals the defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S3 in the catalog); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted, with one ref corrected: dpdp-rules-2025:13(3) was replaced with dpdp-rules-2025:6(1)(b) because Rule 13 binds only a notified Significant Data Fiduciary (not established for example-co) and does not start until 13 May 2027 at the earliest, whereas Rule 6(1)(b) (reasonable safeguards controlling access to computer resources) fits because qa and prod hold pii.","severity":"high","confidence":"confirmed","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S3","dpdp-rules-2025:6(1)(b)"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.AA.S3"},{"regulator":"MeitY","instrument":"dpdp-rules-2025","controlId":"6(1)(b)"},{"regulator":"OWASP","instrument":"owasp-agentic-top10-2026","controlId":"ASI09"},{"regulator":"OWASP","instrument":"owasp-llm-top10-2025","controlId":"LLM06"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"},"location":{"path":"src/elicitation.ts","startLine":30,"endLine":44},"fingerprint":"f658ce80746ca24360bbbc6ea77d7913bf57efcbcb4882305d7036800cecb0f0","source":{"kind":"sarif","ruleId":"AGENT-ASI09-01","tool":"maxwell-agent-graph-auditor","toolVersion":"1.0.0"},"status":"open","slaDueAt":"2026-09-21T19:14:04Z","slaBasis":{"instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.MA.S3","topic":"patch-sla","severity":"high","days":7},"relatedObservationIds":["obs_01M2GPBK5JXJTXXTT6R2YA05PN"],"firstSeenAt":"2026-09-14T19:14:04Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-09-14T19:14:04Z","evidence":[{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/25584b4f-cb91-4da7-9198-1c6516a03390/probe-agent-graph.mcp-gateway.mongodb-