+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2GPBK5MSHBXGGFSRYHPXQY2","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T19:14:04Z","companyId":"example-co","title":"Write/delete MongoDB and Atlas tool categories are enabled by default with no allow-list","description":"src/common/config/userConfig.ts: `readOnly` defaults to false (lines 95-103) and `disabledTools` defaults to an empty array (lines 74-78). src/tools/tool.ts verifyAllowed() (lines 757-783) is the only gate that consults these two values, so a freshly deployed instance exposes every mongodb/atlas create, update and delete tool (createCollection, createIndex, insertMany, deleteMany, dropCollection, dropDatabase, dropIndex, renameCollection, updateMany, atlas-create-db-user, atlas-create-access-list, atlas-streams-manage/teardown, upgradeCluster) unless an operator explicitly sets MDB_MCP_READ_ONLY=true or lists categories/tools in MDB_MCP_DISABLED_TOOLS. Combined with the confirmation bypass in AGENT-ASI09-01, a client without elicitation support can reach delete/drop/create operations on stores classified pii+financial (applications/mcp-gateway/env/qa.json, env/prod.json) with no default guardrail beyond the operator's own deployment configuration, which is outside these assigned roots and therefore not directly verified. Severity is the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S3 (high); confidence is lowered because a deployment could set readOnly/disabledTools at runtime. Refutation: evidence lens not refuted (userConfig.ts disabledTools default [] lines 74-78, readOnly default false lines 95-103; tool.ts verifyAllowed lines 757-783 is the config gate; SARIF result index 1 matches on ruleId, path, lines and fingerprint; the AWS deploy tree sets only MDB_MCP_DISABLED_TOOLS=atlas-local and never MDB_MCP_READ_ONLY; high equals the PR.AA.S3 catalog defaultSeverity; three overstatements corrected: Atlas write tools register only when apiClientId/apiClientSecret are set, tool names in the description are file names rather than registered names, and the deployment config is inside the repo and was checked); regulatory-mapping lens not refuted (sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.AA.S3 applies, is in the catalog with no category narrowing and covers least-privilege for write/delete tools on by default; the ledger control record exists; ASI02 and LLM06 both fit).","severity":"high","confidence":"possible","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S3"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.AA.S3"},{"regulator":"OWASP","instrument":"owasp-agentic-top10-2026","controlId":"ASI02"},{"regulator":"OWASP","instrument":"owasp-llm-top10-2025","controlId":"LLM06"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"mcp-gateway","repoId":"mongodb-mcp-server"},"location":{"path":"src/common/config/userConfig.ts","startLine":74,"endLine":103},"fingerprint":"5e8d5ad607ba7b8c4f85364640afdeca826d84ab45d32b497c7dba48e91dfb3d","source":{"kind":"sarif","ruleId":"AGENT-ASI02-01","tool":"maxwell-agent-graph-auditor","toolVersion":"1.0.0"},"status":"open","slaDueAt":"2026-09-21T19:14:04Z","slaBasis":{"instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.MA.S3","topic":"patch-sla","severity":"high","days":7},"relatedObservationIds":["obs_01M2GPBK5JXJTXXTT6R2YA05PN"],"firstSeenAt":"2026-09-14T19:14:04Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-09-14T19:14:04Z","evidence":[{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/25584b4f-cb91-4da7-9198-1c6516a03390/probe-agent-graph.mcp-gateway.mongodb-mcp-server.sarif.export.json","description":"AGENT-ASI02-01 result, index 1","sha256":"23c9fd39e59293556990c690de7433080e34fcc9162de85a3550553e95fe24e5"}],"tags":["agentic","static-probe","owasp-agentic-top10-2026:asi02","least-privilege"],"provenance":{"harness":"claude-code","generatedAt":"2026-09-14T19:14:04Z","sessionId":"25584b4f-cb91-4da7-9198-1c6516a03390","runId":"run_01M2FGNVVQ15ZKXZWGW74YWAAQ","workflow":"probe-agent-graph","agent":"agent-graph-auditor"}}
