+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"observation","id":"obs_01M2GR10W9092ZYA2BKVFCFTJM","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T19:35:56Z","companyId":"example-co","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.IP.S6"],"title":"V2 Validation and Business Logic: models declare few server-side constraints on identity, amount and privilege fields","description":"ASVS 5.0 L1 scope. The models give callers little validation to rely on:\n- User.user_phone_number (models.py:389) and user_country (422) are unconstrained StringFields.\n- Reward.reward_amount (488) and Holdings.purchase_price and purchase_qty (356-357) have no min_value, so zero or negative amounts pass validation. They are also floats; float money is already recorded by probe-schemas as obs_01M2G24FPP5W96NFAQ6JF098SJ.\n- User.profile_answers (413) and user_binance_auth_creds (397) are DynamicFields that accept any structure.\n- User.user_permission_level (392-394, choices Unauthorized/Authorized/Admin) sits on the same document as profile fields a user can edit. A caller that binds request bodies straight onto User, for example User(**body) or user.update(**body), would allow privilege escalation by mass assignment.\n- ListField(StringField) passes the class instead of an instance (lines 21, 30, 45, 53, 384, 407, 408). Whether mongoengine 0.24.1 still type-checks list items in that case was not verified; mongoengine is not installed and the review was read-only.\nNone of these can be exploited from inside the library because it has no entry points, so no finding is raised. Whether the consuming services validate input is inconclusive. Logic bug noted without a security impact: insight_likes at 277 and 325 always evaluates to 0 or None.","methods":["execute-scr"],"subjects":[{"type":"repo","appId":"db-models","repoId":"onfinance-db-model-master"}],"collectedAt":"2026-09-14T19:35:56Z","expiresAt":"2026-10-14T19:35:56Z","result":"partial","toolOutput":{"format":"sarif","path":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/d39b9417-293b-4271-b6af-ce77f681e83f/execute-s