+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"observation","id":"obs_01M2GR110GMYDRZ29NP7A89CCT","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T19:35:56Z","companyId":"example-co","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S8","cert-in-directions-2022:Dir-iv"],"title":"V16 Security Logging and Error Handling: library emits no logs; error exposure depends on consuming services","description":"ASVS 5.0 L1 scope. The library has no logging, so it cannot log PII, secrets or request bodies. It also has no audit-event responsibility, having no auth or entry points. Error handling observations:\n- fetch_notif_as_dict (models.py:449-473) swallows every exception in two broad except-Exception blocks and falls back to empty entity fields. Nothing is leaked, but the failure is not logged.\n- fetch_insights_as_dict_full dereferences entity.entity_fb_id (309) without a None check after .first() (285), which raises AttributeError when the entity is missing.\n- market_impact_opt[int(self.insight_order//3334)] (273-275, 317-319) raises IndexError for insight_order >= 10002 and wraps silently for negative values.\nWhether these exceptions reach clients as stack traces depends on the consuming services' handlers, which are not in this checkout.","methods":["execute-scr"],"subjects":[{"type":"repo","appId":"db-models","repoId":"onfinance-db-model-master"}],"collectedAt":"2026-09-14T19:35:56Z","expiresAt":"2026-10-14T19:35:56Z","result":"inconclusive","toolOutput":{"format":"sarif","path":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/d39b9417-293b-4271-b6af-ce77f681e83f/execute-scr.db-models.onfinance-db-model-master.sarif.export.json","sha256":"46a0a2106e529443f3fb1eef74299488a7b4aa6cc106ca490d095a35e5bec8a2"},"evidence":[{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/db-models/repos/onfinance-db-model-master/onfinance_db_model_master/models.py","sha256":"7f6eb5d6f2beb71e698ada8a80adaee08fb316afe8d9ed3c25238e33ba46b553","collectedAt":"2026-09-14T19:40:03Z","description":"lines 273-275, 285-309, 317-319, 449-477 at 70b3633e"},{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/d39b9417-293b-4271-b6af-ce77f681e83f/execute-scr.db-models.onfinance-db-model-master.sarif.export.json","sha256":"46a0a2106e529443f3fb1eef74299488a7b4aa6cc106ca490d095a35e5bec8a2","collectedAt":"2026-09-14T19:40:03Z"}],"tags":["scr","scr:v16"],"provenance":{"harness":"claude-code","generatedAt":"2026-09-14T19:35:56Z","sessionId":"d39b9417-293b-4271-b6af-ce77f681e83f","runId":"run_01M2FGNVVQ15ZKXZWGW74YWAAQ","workflow":"execute-scr","agent":"soc-ledger-keeper"}}
+{"schemaVersion":"1","kind":"finding","id":"fnd_01M2GMN61NFQDTRGPZ5RMSMTWN","recordedAt":"2026-09-14T19:35:56Z","companyId":"example-co","supersedes":"fnd_01M2GMN61NFQDTRGPZ5RMSMTWN","title":"db-models: Zerodha password, 2FA secret, API secrets and access tokens stored as plain MongoDB fields","description":"class Secrets(Document) (onfinance_db_model_master/models.py:8-15) declares apiKey, zerodha_username, zerodha_password (line 11), zerodha_2fa (line 12), apiSecrets (line 13) and accessToken (line 14) as plain mongoengine StringField. User.user_binance_auth_creds (line 397) is an open DynamicField holding crypto-exchange credentials.\n\nThe library offers no protection for these fields:\n- no encrypted field type, pre_save/post_init signal, KMS or secrets-manager reference;\n- no helper that stores only a vault locator.\nAny service that uses these models therefore writes broker login secrets and API tokens into MongoDB in a form readable by anyone with collection read access, backups or database logs. That contradicts company policy secretsManagement.backend = aws-secrets-manager.\n\nOnly field names are reported; no secret value is committed in the checkout.\n\nThe rule id and path are reused from the existing ledger finding fnd_01M2GMN61NFQDTRGPZ5RMSMTWN (probe-schemas, same fingerprint 5ecce787...), so the ledger supersedes it rather than duplicating. Code review re-confirms it at pinned commit 70b3633e171a1b8d389b27bb901c84c34a0e9bf6 and adds the secrets-management angle (ASVS 13.3.1). owasp-asvs-5.0:13.3.1 dropped from controlIds: no catalog file exists for owasp-asvs-5.0 to verify the control id against; kept as a secondary regulatoryRef only.\n\nConfidence is likely, not confirmed: a consumer could encrypt values before assignment, and consumer code is not in this repo. Nothing in the model enforces or hints at that.\n\nData flow: consumer service assigns Secrets.zerodha_password / zerodha_2fa / apiSecrets / accessToken (models.py:11-14) or User.user_binance_auth_creds (models.py:397) -> Document.save() via mongoengine StringField/DynamicField (no encryption hook) -> MongoDB collections 'secrets' and 'user' stored as plaintext BSON.\n\nExploit scenario: An attacker or insider obtains read access to the MongoDB deployment used by a consumer of this library, for example through a leaked connection string, a database backup, an over-privileged analytics user, or a NoSQL injection in a consuming API. They run db.secrets.find() and read zerodha_password, zerodha_2fa, apiSecrets and accessToken for every connected account, and db.user.find({}, {user_binance_auth_creds: 1}) for exchange keys. With those they log into customers' Zerodha broking accounts or call exchange APIs to place trades or withdraw.\n\nImpact: Takeover of customers' third-party trading and exchange accounts, with unauthorised trades and financial loss. It would also be a reportable personal data breach under DPDP and a cyber incident under CERT-In and SEBI reporting. The only recorded environment today is dev with exposure isolated and dataClassification internal, and no production deployment of these models is visible. The metastore classifies these fields restricted/spdi. Severity high comes from the catalog defaultSeverity of sebi-cscrf-2024 PR.DS.S1, because this is a storage control gap without a direct exploit in the library, so no CVSS was computed. PR.AA.S1 and dpdp-rules-2025 6(1)(a) also default to high.\n\nRemediation: Do not persist third-party credentials in application documents:\n1. Store broker and exchange API secrets and access tokens in AWS Secrets Manager, per company policy, and keep only a secret ARN or locator field in the model.\n2. Do not store zerodha_password or zerodha_2fa at all; use Kite Connect OAuth-style request and access tokens instead.\n3. Where a token must stay in MongoDB, use MongoDB client-side field-level encryption (CSFLE or Queryable Encryption) with a KMS-held key, or a custom encrypted mongoengine field that encrypts in to_mongo and decrypts in to_python.\n4. Restrict user_binance_auth_creds to a typed EmbeddedDocument holding a locator rather than a DynamicField.\n5. Rotate every credential already stored in any environment's secrets and user collections.","severity":"high","confidence":"likely","controlIds":["sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.DS.S1","sebi-cscrf-2024:PR.AA.S1","dpdp-rules-2025:6(1)(a)"],"regulatoryRefs":[{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.DS.S1"},{"regulator":"SEBI","instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","controlId":"PR.AA.S1"},{"regulator":"MeitY","instrument":"dpdp-rules-2025","controlId":"6(1)(a)"},{"regulator":"OWASP","instrument":"owasp-asvs-5.0","controlId":"13.3.1"}],"target":{"type":"repo","appId":"db-models","repoId":"onfinance-db-model-master"},"location":{"path":"onfinance_db_model_master/models.py","startLine":8,"endLine":15},"fingerprint":"5ecce787cb468f60681fcd1a0b4b7d79e98cf04809d00f455c6048a4b580e376","source":{"kind":"sarif","ruleId":"SCH-PII-02","tool":"maxwell-secure-code-reviewer","toolVersion":"1.0.0"},"status":"open","firstSeenAt":"2026-09-14T18:36:43Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-09-14T19:35:56Z","slaBasis":{"instrument":"sebi-cscrf-2024","days":30},"slaDueAt":"2026-10-14T18:36:43Z","relatedObservationIds":["obs_01M2GR10Y12GJ9R3VB53JSPA8F"],"evidence":[{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/db-models/repos/onfinance-db-model-master/onfinance_db_model_master/models.py","sha256":"7f6eb5d6f2beb71e698ada8a80adaee08fb316afe8d9ed3c25238e33ba46b553","collectedAt":"2026-09-14T19:40:03Z","description":"lines 8-15 (Secrets) and 397 (user_binance_auth_creds) at 70b3633e"},{"type":"workspace-file","ref":"applications/db-models/repos/onfinance-db-model-master/setup.py","sha256":"13c1e68d74d84cd7be239cc2dafec49aebf52c31f4f5048794609cd71d2c11d6","collectedAt":"2026-09-14T19:40:03Z","description":"install_requires only mongoengine==0.24.1; no encryption/KMS dependency"},{"type":"sarif","ref":"kpis/data/raw/sessions/d39b9417-293b-4271-b6af